# The U6+'s storage (the eMMC), the root and data file systems, the layers laid over the system (peakroute-state)
mtk-sd
# the eMMC's 3.3 V supply (the device tree's regulator-3p3v, driver reg-fixed-voltage, module "fixed"): a module in Debian's kernel, without which the eMMC driver waits
# for its supply forever and the root file system never appears
fixed
ext4
overlay
# the kernel's log of a crash is kept in the RAM U-Boot leaves alone (ramoops@42ff0000) and read after the restart
ramoops
# the SoC's watchdog, which U-Boot may leave running: its driver keeps it fed while the system starts (it also resets the Wi-Fi)
mtk_wdt
